Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:16:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence spend-limited claims on every executor
 [daveey]

Problem: home spend holds lost to concurrent foreign ready/review claims.
Why 1: hold() returned on foreign_copy before pending-decision or spend reads
(kanban_spend_budget.py:318-319); worker-a1 performed no spend computation.
Why 2: low-level claim functions fenced containment but not spend decisions.
Why 3: home triage was asynchronously synced; a new live lease rejected status.
Root (happened): spend enforcement existed at home-owned triage, not executor CAS.
Root (not caught): hold/unblock suites omitted foreign pickup and unpublished holds.
Recurrence: #3803 publication sparing and #3819 refusal accounting did not address
claim arbitration. Both contracts and their existing suites remain unchanged.

Prepare a read-only predicate before lease acquisition, then recheck pending stop,
existing spend accounting/card limits and recognised publication identity inside
the claim transaction. PR network reads stay outside the write transaction.
Only home writes triage and decision producers; no budgets/caps/priorities change.

Proof: two-gateway reclaim/hold/claim ready+review regressions fail on old code
and pass after the fix; first exhaustion without a stop is also RED/GREEN.
Focused new tests: 15 passed. Existing nine spend suites: 202 passed unchanged.
Full scripts/check: 21 checks pass after refreshing the stale base.
Retrospective read-only replay refuses all three captured cases, plus worker-a1's
retained copy. Historical current rows are not claim-time DB snapshots; retained
stop evidence proves refusal independently of retrospective run-window counts.

